# Mosquitto ACL example — least-privilege topic access.
#
# Why: the React dashboard ships its MQTT credentials inside the browser JS
# bundle (Vite embeds VITE_MQTT_* at build time), so ANYONE on the network can
# extract them from view-source. Without ACLs those credentials allow full
# publish/subscribe on every topic — including screen power control.
#
# Setup:
#   1. Create one mosquitto user per role (usernames below MUST match):
#        sudo mosquitto_passwd -c mosquitto/config/passwd ha
#        sudo mosquitto_passwd -b mosquitto/config/passwd bot <password>
#        sudo mosquitto_passwd -b mosquitto/config/passwd kiosk <password>
#        sudo mosquitto_passwd -b mosquitto/config/passwd dashboard <password>
#   2. Copy this file to mosquitto/config/acl and edit usernames to match.
#   3. Uncomment the two acl_file lines in mosquitto.conf.
#   4. Use matching credentials in .env (MQTT_USER=bot), presence_config.env
#      (kiosk), and dashboard/.env (dashboard).
#   5. docker compose restart mqtt

# Home Assistant — full control
user ha
topic readwrite #

# Telegram bot — owns the dashboard data topics
user bot
topic readwrite home/dashboard/#
topic read $SYS/#

# Pi Zero 2W presence daemon — publishes sensor data, receives screen commands
user kiosk
topic write home/dashboard/kitchen/presence
topic write homeassistant/#
topic read home/dashboard/kitchen/screen/set

# Browser dashboards — read-only consumers
user dashboard
topic read home/dashboard/#
